deployment.yaml
Defines how Kubernetes runs your application, including which container image to use and how many replicas to maintain.


service.yaml
Gives your application a stable network endpoint so other applications, or sometimes external users, can reach its Pods.


configmap.yaml
Stores non-sensitive configuration, such as application settings or environment-specific values.
it is the settings file for your application.


secret.yaml
store Kubernetes Secret resources for sensitive data, such as passwords and tokens.
it is a credential container.


namespace.yaml
Creates a Kubernetes Namespace, which separates resources into logical groups within a cluster.
it is a workspace or compartment.


hpa.yaml
A Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA), can increase or decrease the number of application Pods based on configured metrics and limits.
it work as automatic capacity adjustment.


ingress.yaml
Defines rules for routing external HTTP/HTTPS traffic to services inside the cluster.
it is a web traffic gateway.


pod.yaml
A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes and can contain one or more containers.
it is a running application unit. 


multiplenamespace.yaml
use to  defines multiple Namespace resources in one file.


node_app & saturday_bankapp 
these are to show my understanding of how cloud concept work and how resource is deployed.
